                    "",
                    "",
                    "",
                    "",
                    "If you say that's just a different joy,<br>And its subtlety is of that nature,<br>If opposing conditions should arise,<br>Would suffering then not come to be?<sup>*</sup> <i class='footnote'>1. An opponent argues that subtle suffering exists but is overwhelmed by great pleasure<br>2. They claim this transforms the suffering into a subtle form of joy<br>3. They use the analogy of a white crystal appearing red when colored by red dust<br>4. The text refutes this by questioning how to distinguish between transformed suffering and natural subtle joy<br>5. It criticizes the attempt to artificially create distinctions where none exist<br>6. It addresses the case of opposing conditions preventing suffering from arising</i>",
